From 7c9d15a482c77e53e823f1ac17e1ca23499875a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Verbovoy <145046797+iverbovoy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:08:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] osd: on a display with a seam, an upright bar beside
 the volume keys that a finger drags

Anchored to the top edge alone the OSD was centred on the output, and the
hinge cut through the volume bar. On a display with a seam it now stands
at the right panel's right edge, beside the volume keys: a 7px bar, drawn
here (a GtkScale gave its trough 11px whatever its CSS asked, and its fill
stood a pixel off it), the level in the accent colour. A finger anywhere
on it sets the volume and it follows the finger - up as well as down, for
a phone whose volume-up key no longer works; the finger keeps it up. It
fades in and out where it stands, and goes 2 s after the last key or
touch, fading from 1.5 s. $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sfduo-osd "<top> <length>"
places it by hand, to try on the device without restarting the shell.
